      "stageRecord": "The subject DP moves from the previously represented Spec-IP position to Spec-CP, leaving an unpronounced DP trace. Its pronounced occurrence now occupies a nonargument position, while the trace retains the chain's Agent position and nominative licensing. Moving the structurally higher wh-argument first implements the superiority requirement for the neutral Bulgarian multiple-wh order. The object remains in its V-complement position at this intermediate stage; its later fronting therefore cannot be mistaken for movement from an already fronted position. The subject landing site enters the wh-licensing configuration with interrogative C. The subject trace is antecedent-governed by the Spec-CP occurrence in this local dependency; the null C introduces no overt-complementizer intervention. This analysis uses traces rather than unpronounced lexical copies.",
